 "poem": "09",
 "title": "Yet, Heard",
 "movement": "HIS FOOTSTEPS, RETRACED",
 "seconds": 18,
 "lines": "She watches us / gather my things to go. / before I go\u2014 / I call on my Father / summon his calming / demeanor / from the yonders / & we walk for years / & travel east toward the sunrises / & retrace his footsteps / now & then. / guiding a settling down / moon\u2014the way / it used to leave / & my tears fall between / the creases in wave / shadows / of the inner harbor\u2014",
